in 1967 the paac sky bus  also known as the transit expressway  revenue line was set to revolutionize  pittsburgh's public transit  it was slick shiny futuristic completely  automated promising a quick and  comfortable ride on tracks elevated  above traffic  the system ran these small automated  buses because back then you were allowed  to call the buses instead of pods  each bus had 28 seats a max speed of 80  kilometers per hour and electric motors  powered by a third rail  now you might say um adam so far this  sounds  suspiciously like a train a very low  capacity and needlessly over  engineered train and that's because it  is more on that in a bit  this kind bus was envisioned as this  sort of gap filler between buses and  subways because trams don't exist  apparently  but in the end it failed to amount to  anything while the port authority of  allegheny county pac supported the  introduction of the sky bus  both the mayor and the governor opposed  it favoring instead a mixture of heavy  and light rail  the demonstrator line opened up in 1967  and turned out to be quite popular  it was quite the novelty for its time  you know a fully automated transit  system for 1967  it's a big deal but after almost a  decade of political battles  funding and support for the skype was  finally evaporated and by 1980 the  demonstrator line was dismantled  completely despite that however the  developer westinghouse went on to build  the miami metro mover afterwards which  is actually operational to this day  and so systems like the sky bus the  miami metro mover and also monorails in  general  are what we call gadget barn now gadget  bones have essentially the same  operational characteristics as regular  trains  they're metal boxes running between  stations on continuous tracks that need  gentle curves and small elevations but  every gadget bond seems to have some  needless twist  that sets it apart from regular trains  mostly for the sake of not being a train  because turns out the techno [ __ ]  factor is very good at attracting public  support and funding  let's say the city center needs to be  connected with a suburb or something  if the city proposes a light rail line  they might get a fair amount of support  with a third of the population screaming  communism  at least in the u.s but if elon musk  comes along and instead proposes the  epic bacon 420 pickle rick pot shuttle  which would be like a normal lighter  line but with half the capacity or  something  he would get positive uncritical global  media coverage for a month  now that being said the sky bus and  gadget bonds in general have the exact  same operational constraints as regular  trains  which means they must also deal with the  exact same problems  speed energy cost comfort capacity  accessibility and safety and if you can  come up with a system that does well in  all these categories  then congratulations you've  revolutionized transportation  unironically  in real life though overcoming one  problem usually results in exacerbating  others  want to have high speeds going above 300  kilometers per hour will skyrocket your  energy use  in all cases you will also need very  straight tracks with minimal curves  which will drive up costs due to land  purchases  do you want to have low energy use  you'll have to decrease speeds or  capacity or build out costly energy  infrastructure like solar farms next to  the tracks or something  want to have low construction costs  you'll have to use existing right away  such as roads which are usually designed  for lower speeds  you will also need to build on ground  level and have ad create crossings  further decreasing speed and safety  and so on and so forth now that being  said most of the problems  can be solved by almost any gadget bond  but at the expense of horrendously  exacerbating another  and so even if your futuristic techno  system does really well  in 6 out of 7 aspects failing on the 7th  is usually enough for your competition  to demolish you  and that's because your competition is  conventional rail  from trims to high speed rail turns out  trains can solve all seven problems  reasonably well  meaning they'll perform exceptionally  well in some aspects while not running  into the red in any others  these kibas would have been somewhat  fast not that energy efficient but  comfortable  safe maybe accessible but very expensive  11 miles of sky bus plus 18 miles of  conventional bus right away costing  twice as much as 28 miles of light rail  it was also laughably bad in terms of  capacity seriously now for perspective  three of these things hooked up together  would seat as many people as  one hungarian suburban passenger car  from the 60s  70s oh wow look we doubled the skybox's  capacity what kind of tactical miracle  is this  contrasts the sky bus with something  proven tried and tested like  conventional light rail  it's reasonably fast energy efficient  comfortable safe  accessible not too expensive and good at  scaling out capacity  any sane public official will take one  look at this and go yep we're doing the  light rail even if the sky bus promises  to improve its characteristics on the  way  because it's just that a promise with no  guarantee for example concerns about the  sky buses switching system remained  unresolved all the way to the end  and the thing is if projects like the  skybus were truly viable  they would bring a complete system to  the competition with all the issues  already worked out completely  because if the idea was viable they  would have no trouble attracting private  funding for research and development  hell even complete [ __ ] like  theranos and juicero could attract  horrendous amounts of investment  a further problem with systems like the  sky bus and gadget bonds in general  is interoperability so over here in city  skylines we have this international  airport which we would like to connect  to this  commercial district with convention  centers stadiums etc and then go further  on to the city center to this train  station  so first off we can do it by building a  gadget bond in this case it's a monorail  so as you can see here the connection is  up and running and it is possible to get  from the airport to the commercial  district and then to the train station  all three are neatly linked up by the  monorail alright so let's now try doing  the same thing with conventional rail  and see what happens  now the thing about conventional rail is  that while the monorail was this sort of  island service existing completely  separately from all other transit  conventional rail can be neatly  integrated into the existing system  and this is actually pretty good because  now we can have all kinds of trains  stopped by the airport you know if you  have some suburban trains or long  distance trains coming in from the west  they can just stop by the airport and  offload the passengers who want to fly  instead of you know having to travel all  the way to the central station and then  there change to a monorail which then  will take them to the airport  and if you want to go from the airport  to the commercial district then you can  take some rapid bus service or something  when it's not that far away  but beyond issues like feasibility and  interoperability  gadget bonds have one less fatal flaw  it's that  they are built to solve the wrong  problem so let's ask ourselves the  question  why do we want to build things like the  sky bus the loop the miami metro mover  monorails and other gadget bonds well so  that we can travel quickly above the  congested streets  but why are the streets congested well  because we gave them over to cars  so instead of trying to come up with  elaborate over-engineered solutions to  traffic issues  why not start addressing the real  problem why not try to cut back on car  use it worked in london  paris barcelona stockholm vienna and it  will work in the us  even in west coast cities let's take  away a few lanes from cars and turn them  into dedicated lanes for public transit  suddenly we no longer need to build  elaborate elevated track systems  we can just put some tracks in the  middle or some bus lanes on the sides  and the best part is taking away lanes  from cars inhibitor public transit will  decrease congestion because induced  demand works the other way around as  well  building a sky bus or monorail or any  other techno miracle system to fix urban  mobility is like taking painkillers  against a brain tumor  it might help with some of the symptoms  but the tumor will keep taking more and  more space inside your skull  until you die that's my metaphor for a  city becoming unlivable  and this is why the sky bus and other  gadget bounce systems are basically  pointless they are shiny futuristic  half-paid solutions to the wrong problem  if we really want to quote unquote fixed  traffic we need to  a cut back car use drastically so and b  build a [ __ ] train which pittsburgh  actually did in the end so good for them  every other solution is just a band-aid  on a bullet wound basically  a shiny band-aid with the occasional  gamer lights  thank you for watching please like and  subscribe if you haven't already and i  would also like to thank my patrons for  helping me run this channel  and if you also want to support me  through patreon the link is down in the  description  thank you for watching and see you next  time  you
 

